codex
The canonical closure has 10 rules. Nine are direct macro/function equations. The one `simplification` rule refines `applyCmp`; Stage 1 compiles it into `verification-kompiled` before any `kprove` invocation and never proves its exact statement in a rule-free module. Under this stage’s stricter taxonomy, that rule is a `DOMAIN_LEMMA`, not a proved derived lemma.
